{
  "id": "Compound::DB00547 - Gene::2908",
  "verbalization": "Desoximetasone, a corticosteroid hormone receptor agonist, is linked to Nr3c1 through a series of molecular pathways that converge on the nuclear receptor subfamily 3, member 1 (Nr3c1). The evidence suggests that Desoximetasone, as part of the broader class of corticosteroid hormone receptor agonists, binds to Nr3c1 through a shared mechanism involving the 21-hydroxy steroid pathway. This pathway is a common route for corticosteroids to exert their effects, and all three compounds—Desoximetasone, Prednicarbate, and Alclometasone—share a common ancestor in the therapeutic glucocorticoid category. The binding of these compounds to Nr3c1 is supported by the presence of a lowest common ancestor in the 21-hydroxy steroid pathway, indicating a conserved molecular interaction. The integration of these pathways highlights a recurring mechanism where corticosteroid agonists interact with Nr3c1 through a shared biological pathway, suggesting a unified role in the regulation of gene expression via glucocorticoid receptors.",
